From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:51:47 -0400
Subject: feat: the address field's width as a setting, and no Ask Google line

GitHub issue 14 (toolbar T48, privacy Q17). Settings > Stedding > Address
field offers Full width, the default (T29), or a field centred on the page
at 800, 640 or 480 DIP. A centred field keeps its width and place in every
state, the suggestions open under it at its width, and the empty row either
side of it moves the window: the two spacers are views of their own class
that the caption hit test passes through. The spacers now always exist and
are shown with a centred width; a change applies at once. A positive
`location_bar_width` still overrides the setting. Once the field is moved
onto the page's middle the spacers are set to fill the row either side of
it, so neither lies over the field's end: on Windows the field moves
toward the caption buttons, and the right spacer took the presses of the
buttons at its end, Copy Link among them (issue 14, BACKLOG S-357).

In a side-by-side split the field is the active pane's (toolbar T49, a
comment on issue 14 after 0.4.0 beta 2): over that pane alone, full width
taking its part of the row and a centred width centred on it, no wider. It
had spanned both panes, the left pane's address drawn across the gap. The
row lays out again when the panes move (the window background already
watches them) and when the active tab changes.

The focused field no longer offers "Ask Google about this page" with
Google as the engine: Chromium's OmniboxContextualSearchOnFocusSuggestions
is off, as the rest of that family already was.

Why: the owner asked for both on 2026-10-28, and for the split's field on
2026-10-30.
Removable when: never as a feature; the toolbar hunks go if Chromium's
toolbar grows its own width setting.
